      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x-1&=\\frac{1-2t-t^2}{1+t^2}\\\\(x-1)^2+y^2&=\\frac{(1-t^2-2t)^2+(1-t^2+2t)^2}{(1+t^2)^2}\\\\(x-1)^2+y^2&=\\frac{2(1-t^2)^2+8t^2}{(1+t^2)^2}\\\\(x-1)^2+y^2&=2\\end{align*}$$\nIf $x=0$, then $t=1$ and $y=1$, so $(0,-1)$ is excluded.\nTo check for further restrictions, write $S=x+y+1$ and $D=y-x+1$. On the circle,\n$$\\begin{align*}S^2+D^2&=4S\\\\S-D&=2x\\end{align*}$$\nThe equation $S=0$ on this circle gives only $(0,-1)$. For every other point, set $t=\\frac{D}{S}$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2-2t}{1+t^2}&=\\frac{2S(S-D)}{S^2+D^2}=x\\\\\\frac{1+2t-t^2}{1+t^2}&=\\frac{S^2+2SD-D^2}{S^2+D^2}=y\\end{align*}$$\nThus the curve is $(x-1)^2+y^2=2$, excluding only $(0,-1)$.",
